and beyond that, also talk
to big data systems, or data

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:34.720
lakes, where when you're doing
something like a data lineage

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.147
or impact analysis.

00:14:36.147 --> 00:14:37.730
It's not enough if
you're just looking

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:40.970
at your traditional relational
data which is primarily

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:43.100
data at rest, but
you also want to look

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:44.855
at the data in
motion, which could

00:14:44.855 --> 00:14:47.450
be data coming from IOT stream.

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:48.840
It could be coming
from web logs.

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:50.940
It could be social media data.

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:54.820
So how do I bring that lineage
across my different artifacts,

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:58.270
starting from a BI
dashboard or analytics

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:01.160
report that I'm looking
at, and try to point that

00:15:01.160 --> 00:15:04.170
to a source of origin
which could be, hey,

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:06.810
this data came from
SAP ERP system.

00:15:06.810 --> 00:15:11.610
But now it is residing in an
HDFS file as a Parquet format.

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:15.530
So it's very important for us to
combine these two worlds, which

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:17.420
is the on-prem and the
cloud, and especially

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:20.270
when we talk about these
multi-cloud environments,

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:23.420
and support different
kinds of workloads.

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:25.760
Like I said, it could be
the IOT streaming workloads,

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:28.190
or it could be advanced
analytics, which

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:30.980
has now migrated to the
whole machine learning

00:15:30.980 --> 00:15:33.200
AI kind of workloads.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.405
And finally, a
basic cloud storage,

00:15:35.405 --> 00:15:38.390
where I'm looking
at a data aging,

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:39.990
data tiering
strategy, where I want

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:45.240
to push my cold data into
a cloud or a frozen state.

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:48.740
So how do I ensure that I
build a pipeline which can also

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:51.050
bring in the data
from a frozen state,

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:53.870
combine that with hot
data, in-memory data,

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:55.700
that we have in
SAP HANA, which is

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:58.665
our central core of
the digital platform?

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:05.280
So we have collaborated with
Google on multiple aspects.

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:06.930
But one of the
primary things here

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:11.560
